      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a note for the dev team.\n\nCiting from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myriad#East_Asia\n\n> In East Asia, the traditional numeral systems of China, Korea, and Japan are all decimal-based but grouped into ten thousands rather than thousands.\n\nSo, in daily life, we Japanese people usually use\n\n- \"万\" : 10^4 = 10000 \n\n- \"億\" : 10^8 = 100000000 \n\ninstead of SI prefixes https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_System_of_Units#Prefixes\n\n- kilo \"k\" : 10^3 = 1000\n\n- mega \"M\" : 10^6 = 1000000\n\nPeople learn SI prefixes at school, so they should know them, but the actual usage in society is limited somewhat to the technical area.\n\nAdditional 1: This issue is not just a matter of the string but may include calculations, so I guess this is not an easy task to implement.\n\nAdditional 2:  BTW, in the English presentation (as captured in the attached image), the kilo should be a lower letter \"k\" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilo-\n\nAdditional 3: This is an unnecessary addition. Strictly and technically speaking, those are not units as in the post's title.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
